
def 0 {
    lives(ACTOR_PLAYER);
    SetAnimation(2);
    lives(ACTOR_ATTENDANT1);
    SetAnimation(2);
    message_Notice({
        english="""
            
            [CN]All sorts of information is written here...
        """,
    });
    message_Close();
    message_ResetActor();
    flag_Set($EVENT_LOCAL, 8);
    message_Menu(MENU_GUILD_F_A_Q_BOARD);
    Case(1, @label_0);
    Case(2, @label_1);
    Case(3, @label_2);
    Case(4, @label_3);
    Case(5, @label_4);
    Case(6, @label_5);
    Case(7, @label_6);
    Case(8, @label_7);
    Jump(@label_8);
    @label_0;
    message_Mail({
        english="[CN]Q1: About Explorers of Alpha",
    });
    message_Mail({
        english="""
            Explorers of Alpha is the first difficulty and
            Quality of Life hack based on Explorers of Sky.
        """,
    });
    message_Mail({
        english="""
            The game is under development since mid-2020
            and has received special attention in game and
            level-design while being developed.
        """,
    });
    message_Mail({
        english="""
            At first the aim of the hack was to have an
            Arceus event as the final challenge of the
            game, but it more turned out as THE QoL-hack.
        """,
    });
    message_Mail({
        english="""
            Things to note about the game are that all the
            stuff in it is original, and credited when it's
            not, and that I wrote my own patches for it.
        """,
    });
    message_Mail({
        english="""
            New events, features and adjustments are my
            only doing, so if you see the same features in
            similar hacks, they're likely taken from mine.
        """,
    });
    message_Mail({
        english="""
            More than a SkyTemple patches showcase, it's
            a QoL-hack with new events, quests, and
            features you can expect from a polished hack.
        """,
    });
    message_Mail({
        english="...What a good read!",
    });
    JumpCommon(CORO_END_TALK);
    @label_1;
    message_Mail({
        english="[CN]Q2: What are the different difficulties for?",
    });
    message_Mail({
        english="""
            [CN]In Alpha you can choose to play at different
            [CN]levels of difficulty. The higher the difficulty,
            [CN]the stronger the enemies are.
        """,
    });
    message_Mail({
        english="""
            [CN]You may also lower the difficulty as you wish,
            [CN]however you cannot return to a more difficult
            [CN]setting if you do so in Hardcore or Expert.
        """,
    });
    @label_15;
    message_Mail({
        english="[CN]Which difficulty do you want to check?",
    });
    message_SwitchMenu(0, 1);
    CaseMenu({
        english="Vanilla",
    }, @label_9);
    CaseMenu({
        english="[CS:A]Difficult[CR]",
    }, @label_10);
    CaseMenu({
        english="[CS:H]Expert[CR]",
    }, @label_11);
    CaseMenu({
        english="[CS:B]Hardcore[CR]",
    }, @label_12);
    CaseMenu({
        english="None",
    }, @label_13);
    Jump(@label_14);
    @label_9;
    message_Mail({
        english="[CN]About Vanilla mode",
    });
    message_Mail({
        english="""
            [CN]More in line with the original game. If you
            [CN]want to experience Alpha without ever feeling
            [CN]the need to grind, this difficulty is for you.
        """,
    });
    message_Mail({
        english="""
            [CN]Most of the added difficulty such as
            [CN]Field Effects or dojo anti-abuse will
            [CN]also be disabled for you.
        """,
    });
    Jump(@label_15);
    @label_10;
    message_Mail({
        english="[CS:A][CN]About Difficult mode[CR]",
    });
    message_Mail({
        english="""
            [CN]Slightly harder than your average Mystery
            [CN]Dungeon game, with additions specifically
            [CN]made for Explorers of Alpha available to you.
        """,
    });
    Jump(@label_15);
    @label_11;
    message_Mail({
        english="[CS:H][CN]About Expert mode[CR]",
    });
    message_Mail({
        english="""
            [CN]All the difficulty from previous versions with
            [CN]Alpha 2.0 additions and rebalancing.
        """,
    });
    message_Mail({
        english="""
            [CN]This used to be the original difficulty of the
            [CN]game and is still the default one in Alpha 2.0.
        """,
    });
    Jump(@label_15);
    @label_12;
    message_Mail({
        english="[CS:B][CN]About Hardcore mode[CR]",
    });
    message_Mail({
        english="""
            [CN]Expert but everything goes wrong. This game
            [CN]mode is designed to be a near impossible task.
        """,
    });
    message_Mail({
        english="""
            [CN]Higher spawn rate, higher enemy density,
            [CN]higher trap density, forced scaling in both
            [CN]stats and moves, aggressive anti-cheat...
        """,
    });
    message_Mail({
        english="""
            [CN]At many points it will feel like an unfair or
            [CN]tedious challenge. This was the intent so
            [CN]prepare yourself to lose many many times!
        """,
    });
    Jump(@label_15);
    @label_13;
    message_Mail({
        english="...What a good read!",
    });
    JumpCommon(CORO_END_TALK);
    @label_14;
    Jump(@label_13);
    @label_2;
    message_Mail({
        english="[CN]Q3: How do special challenges work?",
    });
    message_Mail({
        english="""
            [CN]In Alpha you can take on different challenges.
            [CN]They are here to offer a different way to play
            [CN]the game, far from the usual PMD experience.
        """,
    });
    message_Mail({
        english="""
            [CN]You can select one challenge, and toggle
            [CN]different options for your challenge run.
            [CN]Toggleable options are shown with a [M:S3] mark.
        """,
    });
    message_Mail({
        english="""
            [CN]You can forfeit your challenge when you want.
            [CN]If you do, however, you cannot select another
            [CN]challenge until you finish the main story.
        """,
    });
    message_Mail({
        english="""
            [CN]The challenge automatically ends after you
            [CN]beat the game, so when the story is over.
        """,
    });
    message_Mail({
        english="""
            [CN]Some challenges are unlocked again by beating
            [CN]the corresponding endgame dungeon.
        """,
    });
    @label_24;
    message_Mail({
        english="[CN]Which challenge do you want more details on?",
    });
    message_SwitchMenu(0, 1);
    CaseMenu({
        english="Glass Cannon",
    }, @label_16);
    CaseMenu({
        english="Pacifist",
    }, @label_17);
    CaseMenu({
        english="Time Attack",
    }, @label_18);
    CaseMenu({
        english="One Item",
    }, @label_19);
    CaseMenu({
        english="Speedrun",
    }, @label_20);
    CaseMenu({
        english="[M:S3] Options",
    }, @label_21);
    CaseMenu({
        english="None",
    }, @label_22);
    Jump(@label_23);
    @label_16;
    message_Mail({
        english="""
            [CN]Glass Cannon: you will always be at death's
            [CN]doorstep! Your defensive stats are minimized,
            [CN]but your offensive stats are maximized.
        """,
    });
    Jump(@label_24);
    @label_17;
    message_Mail({
        english="""
            [CN]Pacifist: you cannot use attacking moves nor
            [CN]use orbs, however your defensive stats are
            [CN]maximized. Also called No Attack challenge.
        """,
    });
    Jump(@label_24);
    @label_18;
    message_Mail({
        english="""
            [CN]Time Attack: you take damages as turns pass
            [CN]and are prevented from healing by anything
            [CN]except Reviver Seeds.
        """,
    });
    Jump(@label_24);
    @label_19;
    message_Mail({
        english="""
            [CN]One Item: you travel with a one-item bag. You
            [CN]can't have more items in the bag so think
            [CN]carefully about what that one item will be.
        """,
    });
    Jump(@label_24);
    @label_20;
    message_Mail({
        english="""
            [CN]Speedrun: the bag you get at the start has all
            [CN]the needed items for a speedrun. Text is
            [CN]instantaneous so you blast through cutscenes.
        """,
    });
    message_Mail({
        english="""
            [CN]At any point, you can ask [CS:G]Porygon2[CR] to get useful
            [CN]items such as Reviver Seeds or an item bag.
        """,
    });
    Jump(@label_24);
    @label_21;
    message_Mail({
        english="[CN]Know more about Challenge Options here",
    });
    message_SwitchMenu(0, 1);
    CaseMenu({
        english="[M:S3] Recruit 'em all",
    }, @label_25);
    CaseMenu({
        english="[M:S3] Solo-run",
    }, @label_26);
    CaseMenu({
        english="[M:S3] God Mode",
    }, @label_27);
    CaseMenu({
        english="Check Challenges",
    }, @label_24);
    Jump(@label_22);
    @label_25;
    message_Mail({
        english="""
            [CN]Recruit 'em all: Recruitment is guaranteed
            [CN]for species you haven't recruited yet,
            [CN]impossible for other species.
        """,
    });
    Jump(@label_21);
    @label_26;
    message_Mail({
        english="""
            [CN]Solo-run: You can freely choose to enter
            [CN]dungeon with either your leader or partner.
        """,
    });
    message_Mail({
        english="""
            [CN]Remember that you can use Chimecho's swap
            [CN]members feature before Post-Game to enter
            [CN]dungeon with the member you want.
        """,
    });
    Jump(@label_21);
    @label_27;
    message_Mail({
        english="""
            [CN]God-Mode: available if you select Speedrun,
            [CN]or 100% cleared the game by beating the final
            [CN]dungeon new to 2.0.
        """,
    });
    message_Mail({
        english="""
            [CN]This mode gives you passive Mobile Scarf,
            [CN]double speed, X-Ray Specs, Goggle Specs
            [CN]and Tight Belt effects.
        """,
    });
    Jump(@label_21);
    @label_22;
    message_Mail({
        english="...What a good read!",
    });
    JumpCommon(CORO_END_TALK);
    Jump(@label_3);
    @label_23;
    Jump(@label_22);
    @label_3;
    message_Mail({
        english="[CN]Q4: What’s the Level Scaling Option?",
    });
    message_Mail({
        english="""
            [CN]Level scaling is a toggleable option that affects
            [CN]the enemy Pokémon's levels. The effect
            [CN]differs based on the difficulty you set.
        """,
    });
    message_Mail({
        english="""
            [CN]Vanilla: enemy levels will match your level
            [CN]even if your level is lower than the enemy's.
        """,
    });
    message_Mail({
        english="""
            [CS:A][CN]Difficult: Enemy levels will always match your
            [CN]highest level Pokémon.[CR]
        """,
    });
    message_Mail({
        english="""
            [CS:H][CN]Expert: Enemy levels match your highest level
            [CN]Pokémon. If the dungeon level is higher, that
            [CN]value is taken instead.[CR]
        """,
    });
    message_Mail({
        english="""
            [CS:B][CN]Hardcore: Same as Expert, but you can't toggle
            [CN]this option off. That's intended![CR]
        """,
    });
    message_Mail({
        english="...What a good read!",
    });
    JumpCommon(CORO_END_TALK);
    @label_4;
    message_Mail({
        english="[CN]Q5: What does Sandbox Mode stand for?",
    });
    message_Mail({
        english="""
            [CN]Sandbox Mode is a mode added to help the
            [CN]player to get rid of the grindy part of the
            [CN]game, it's essentially a minimal grinding mode.
        """,
    });
    message_Mail({
        english="""
            [CN]Once this option is unlocked, you are given
            [CN]access to any basic supply you want via a new
            [CN]option in both maingame and Special Episodes.
        """,
    });
    message_Mail({
        english="""
            [CN]When toggled on, check with Porygon2 to
            [CN]make use of Sandbox Mode features.
        """,
    });
    message_Mail({
        english="""
            [CN]A shop is at your disposal in maingame which
            [CN]sells useful items for very low cost.
        """,
    });
    message_Mail({
        english="""
            [CN]A bag similar to the one in the Speedrun option
            [CN]in Special Episodes serves the same purpose.
        """,
    });
    message_Mail({
        english="""
            [CN]If not unlocked but enabled, please note
            [CN]your save file will be deleted once you've
            [CN]finished the full story. That's intended!
        """,
    });
    message_Mail({
        english="...What a good read!",
    });
    JumpCommon(CORO_END_TALK);
    @label_5;
    message_Mail({
        english="[CN]Q6: About Exp. Share functionality?",
    });
    message_Mail({
        english="""
            [CN]Exp. Share is an added mechanic that allows
            [CN]Pokémon you haven't brought into a dungeon to
            [CN]receive Exp. from defeated enemies.
        """,
    });
    message_Mail({
        english="""
            [CN]It can be bought and then upgraded by talking
            [CN]to [CS:G]Porygon2[CR] at [CS:P]Crossroads[CR]. The upgrades
            [CN]increase the share standby Pokémon receive.
        """,
    });
    message_Mail({
        english="...What a good read!",
    });
    JumpCommon(CORO_END_TALK);
    @label_6;
    message_Mail({
        english="[CN]Q7: About [CS:G]Porygon2[CR]?",
    });
    message_Mail({
        english="""
            [CN][CS:G]Porygon2[CR] is a very rare Pokémon usually
            [CN]not to be seen around these parts. As such,
            [CN][CS:G]Porygon2[CR]'s services are very unique!
        """,
    });
    message_Mail({
        english="""
            [CN]They are known to offer a large amount
            [CN]of upgrades depending on your [CS:X]Explorer Rank[CR],
            [CN]though they don't tell much about the detail.
        """,
    });
    message_Mail({
        english="""
            [CN]Well... As far as we know, they pretty much
            [CN]don't talk at all! The ones we found in Towns
            [CN]and the others in Dungeons never replied!
        """,
    });
    message_Mail({
        english="""
            [CN]However, we have written a notice relative
            [CN]to the full array of utilities they provide and
            [CN]the [CS:X]Rank[CR] necessary to unlock every single one.
        """,
    });
    message_Mail({
        english="""
            [CS:X]Bronze Rank[CR] -> Daily Money Reward
            [CS:X]Silver Rank[CR] -> Daily buyable Reviver Seeds
            [CS:X]Gold Rank[CR] -> Exp. Boosters upgrades
            [CS:X]Diamond Rank[CR] -> Berries recovery upgrades
            [CS:X]Emerald Rank[CR] -> Stat Bands upgrades
            [CS:X]Expert Rank[CR] -> Mission Board reset
            [CS:X]Ace Rank[CR] -> Ammo upgrades
            [CS:X]Master Rank[CR] -> Vitamins upgrades
            [CS:X]Perfect Rank[CR] -> Gummies upgrades
            [CS:X]Alpha Rank[CR] -> HP Boosters upgrades
            [CS:X]Guildmaster Rank[CR] -> Rare Items shop
            [CS:X]Earth Rank[CR] -> Overdrive Upgrades
        """,
    });
    message_Mail({
        english="...What a good read!",
    });
    JumpCommon(CORO_END_TALK);
    @label_7;
    message_Mail({
        english="[CN]Credits for Explorers of Alpha",
